# concrete-ci-2 — Hetzner AX102 (dedicated), 65.109.50.173. Arch Linux.
# Ryzen 9 7950X3D 16c/32t, 125 GB RAM, 2x 1.7 TB NVMe in md RAID1.
# The image comes up as archlinux-latest-64-minimal; set the name once:
#   hostnamectl set-hostname concrete-ci-2
#
# Role: CI (concrete's landing tier) plus the caches CI reads. GitHub self-hosted runners
# (label `concrete`, light pool `concrete-light`), the Lean seed cache (lakecache), the signed
# Nix binary cache (localhost only), and `CONCRETE_REMOTE=hetzner` gate runs (dev). Since
# 2026-10-26 the fuzz farm, perf and leanprof run on concrete-ci-3, so this host's CPU goes to
# CI alone (and compile-time measurements here are not disturbed by the farm).
# Runners: 6 (16 cores; Lean builds are memory-heavy, ~20 GB each).
ROLE="CI runners + caches"
USERS="dev agent lakecache"
# The repository the runners serve (runners.sh). The owner approved moving concrete to
# lambdaclass/concrete (2026-11-06): the runners move in stages with a per-invocation
# CONCRETE_RUNNER_REPO=lambdaclass/concrete RUNNER_REINSTALL=1 (runners.sh header), 7-8, then 4-6,
# then 1-3, and this line becomes lambdaclass/concrete once all eight have moved. Until then it
# states where they are, so apply.sh changes nothing.
CONCRETE_RUNNER_REPO=unbalancedparentheses/concrete2
RUNNERS="1 2 3 4 5 6"
# The light pool (label concrete-light): Branch health only, so the ~500 per-push
# fast-gate runs a day never take a landing-tier runner from a train. Two runners:
# a run is ~2 min and a later push to the same branch cancels the earlier one.
LIGHT_RUNNERS="7 8"
# Caps for all runners together (concrete-runners.slice, runners.sh; concrete ISS-0007,
# 2026-11-06): at most 24 of 32 CPU-equivalents and 96 GB; the rest is headroom (not reserved) for user.slice.
# Per runner: a landing runner may use 28 GB (a Lean build is ~20 GB), a light runner 4 cores, 8 GB.
CONCRETE_RUNNERS_CPU_QUOTA=2400%
CONCRETE_RUNNERS_MEMORY_MAX=96G
CONCRETE_RUNNERS_TASKS_MAX=16384
CONCRETE_RUNNER_MEMORY_MAX=28G
CONCRETE_LIGHT_RUNNER_MEMORY_MAX=8G
CONCRETE_LIGHT_RUNNER_CPU_QUOTA=400%
SERVICES="lean-cache nix-cache"
# Moved to concrete-ci-3 (2026-10-26). `retire` stops and disables their units and keeps the
# data: /home/fuzz (the user stays; findings, state and the concrete-ci-1 archive), ~dev/perf.
RETIRED_SERVICES="fuzz-farm perf leanprof-profile"
# SSH and mosh over Tailscale only (base.sh / base-arch.sh, servers/ssh-tailscale-only.sh).
SSH_TAILSCALE_ONLY=1
#!/bin/bash
# GitHub Actions self-hosted runners for lambdaclass/stabileo. On a host of Stabileo's own they
# come from apply.sh (STABILEO_RUNNERS in hosts/<host>.env); on a shared host, run as root:
#   gh api -X POST repos/lambdaclass/stabileo/actions/runners/registration-token --jq .token \
#     | ssh admin@65.109.50.173 sudo dotfiles-servers/runners-stabileo.sh 1 2 3
# The token arrives on stdin, is never echoed or stored, and is only read when a runner is not
# registered yet. Idempotent; DRY_RUN=1 to preview.
#
# On a host shared with concrete, concrete comes first and everything here is a guest (the
# defaults below; a guest install on concrete-ci-2 was planned and cancelled 2026-10-23):
# - Users sghaN (home 750, own group, no sudo), runner in ~sghaN/actions-runner-N, name
#   <hostname>-sghaN, persistent. Labels self-hosted,Linux,X64 plus the pool's:
#     ci       stabileo (merge queue, pushes to main), and stabileo-pr too for the runners in
#              STABILEO_PR_RUNNERS (this repo's pull requests); the rest stay the queue's own
#     timing   stabileo-timing (jobs that time themselves): STABILEO_TIMING_RUNNERS, each pinned
#              to its STABILEO_TIMING_CPUS_<N>, cores no other runner gets
#     nightly  stabileo-nightly (nightly fuzzing): STABILEO_NIGHTLY_RUNNERS, low CPU weight
#   Labels are set at registration. To move a registered runner, change its labels with
#   gh api (README.md, "stabileo-ci-1 runner pools") or remove and register it again.
# - All of them run under stabileo-runners.slice: at most 6 cores and 32 GB together by default,
#   and half concrete's CPU and IO weight, so a busy Stabileo queue never starves concrete's
#   runners. Six cores also stays under the fuzz farm's pause threshold (FUZZ_PAUSE_OTHER_CORES=8).
#   Each pool has a child slice (stabileo-runners-<pool>.slice).
# - stabileo-runner-watchdog.timer restarts one runner that hangs (stabileo-runner-watchdog.sh).
# - PrivateTmp + NoNewPrivileges, and a root-owned job-started hook that empties the runner's
#   private /tmp, as for concrete's runners.
# - Package installs and service starts go through lib.sh's guard_runners: nothing here runs
#   while one of concrete's runner jobs is active.
# - Stabileo is public. These runners take only trusted work: its workflows use them for the
#   merge queue and pushes to main, never for pull_request jobs, and the repo requires approval
#   for all external contributors (approval_policy=all_external_contributors, 2026-10-23).
set -euo pipefail
. "$(dirname "$0")/lib.sh"
need_root
[ "$#" -gt 0 ] || die "usage: runners-stabileo.sh N..."

REPO_URL=https://github.com/lambdaclass/stabileo
VER=2.338.1
SHA=08e9ccb3604d2462c24b5e33604dc30810296ca15cc65f23cffd4317eb144c37
TB=/opt/actions-runner-dist/actions-runner-linux-x64-$VER.tar.gz
LIBDIR=/usr/local/lib/stabileo-runner
HOOK=$LIBDIR/job-started.sh
PREFLIGHT=$LIBDIR/preflight.sh
SLICE=stabileo-runners.slice
WATCHDOG_CONF=/etc/stabileo-runner/watchdog.conf
TOKEN=

in_list() { [[ " $2 " == *" $1 "* ]]; }
pool_of() {
  if in_list "$1" "${STABILEO_TIMING_RUNNERS:-}"; then echo timing
  elif in_list "$1" "${STABILEO_NIGHTLY_RUNNERS:-}"; then echo nightly
  else echo ci; fi
}
labels_of() {
  case $(pool_of "$1") in
    timing) echo stabileo-timing ;;
    nightly) echo stabileo-nightly ;;
    *) if in_list "$1" "${STABILEO_PR_RUNNERS:-}"; then echo stabileo,stabileo-pr; else echo stabileo; fi ;;
  esac
}
max_minutes_of() {
  case $(pool_of "$1") in
    timing) echo "${STABILEO_WATCHDOG_TIMING_MIN:-60}" ;;
    nightly) echo "${STABILEO_WATCHDOG_NIGHTLY_MIN:-200}" ;;
    *) echo "${STABILEO_WATCHDOG_CI_MIN:-170}" ;;
  esac
}
cpus_exist() {
  local r c
  for r in $(echo "$1" | tr ',' ' '); do
    for c in $(seq "${r%-*}" "${r#*-}"); do [ -d "/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu$c" ] || return 1; done
  done
}

if ! [ -f "$TB" ]; then
  run install -d -m 755 /opt/actions-runner-dist
  run curl -sSfL -o "$TB.part" "https://github.com/actions/runner/releases/download/v$VER/actions-runner-linux-x64-$VER.tar.gz"
  if [ "$DRY_RUN" != 1 ]; then
    echo "$SHA  $TB.part" | sha256sum -c - && mv "$TB.part" "$TB"
  fi
fi

# Stabileo's Rust jobs link with clang + mold on Linux (engine/.cargo/config.toml). On GitHub's
# runners the workflow installs mold itself, with sudo; here it is part of the host.
command -v mold >/dev/null || run pacman -S --needed --noconfirm mold

[ -d "$LIBDIR" ] || run install -d -m 755 -o root -g root "$LIBDIR"
# What a Stabileo job relies on from the host, checked before a runner registers and at the
# start of every job, so a broken host fails one job with a named cause.
write_file "$PREFLIGHT" 755 root:root <<'X' || true
#!/bin/sh
fail() { echo "stabileo runner preflight FAILED on $(hostname -s): $*" >&2; exit 1; }
for c in git clang mold python3 tar curl; do command -v "$c" >/dev/null || fail "$c not on PATH"; done
X
write_file "$HOOK" 755 root:root <<'X' || true
#!/bin/sh
# /tmp is private to this runner service (PrivateTmp=true), so emptying it touches no other process.
find /tmp -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -user "$(id -u)" -exec rm -rf {} + 2>/dev/null || true
exec /usr/local/lib/stabileo-runner/preflight.sh
X

# The fence. Defaults are a guest's on concrete's CI host; a host of Stabileo's own sets wider
# limits in its hosts/<host>.env (STABILEO_CPU_QUOTA, …), which apply.sh passes through.
TIMING_CPUS=
for N in ${STABILEO_TIMING_RUNNERS:-}; do
  v=STABILEO_TIMING_CPUS_$N
  [ -n "${!v:-}" ] || die "timing runner $N has no $v"
  cpus_exist "${!v}" || die "$v=${!v}: no such CPU on this host"
  TIMING_CPUS=${TIMING_CPUS:+$TIMING_CPUS,}${!v}
done
[ -z "${STABILEO_SHARED_CPUS:-}" ] || cpus_exist "$STABILEO_SHARED_CPUS" || die "STABILEO_SHARED_CPUS=$STABILEO_SHARED_CPUS: no such CPU on this host"

reload=0
write_file "/etc/systemd/system/$SLICE" 644 root:root <<X && reload=1
[Unit]
Description=Stabileo's GitHub Actions runners

[Slice]
CPUQuota=${STABILEO_CPU_QUOTA:-600%}
CPUWeight=${STABILEO_CPU_WEIGHT:-50}
IOWeight=${STABILEO_IO_WEIGHT:-50}
MemoryHigh=${STABILEO_MEMORY_HIGH:-28G}
MemoryMax=${STABILEO_MEMORY_MAX:-32G}
X
# CPUWeight, MemoryHigh and MemoryMax per pool share the parent's limits above.
pool_slice() {  # pool_slice POOL CPUS WEIGHT HIGH MAX
  write_file "/etc/systemd/system/stabileo-runners-$1.slice" 644 root:root <<X && reload=1
[Unit]
Description=Stabileo's GitHub Actions runners: $1 pool

[Slice]
${2:+AllowedCPUs=$2
}CPUWeight=$3
MemoryHigh=$4
MemoryMax=$5
X
}
pool_slice ci "${STABILEO_SHARED_CPUS:-}" 100 "${STABILEO_CI_MEMORY_HIGH:-${STABILEO_MEMORY_HIGH:-28G}}" "${STABILEO_CI_MEMORY_MAX:-${STABILEO_MEMORY_MAX:-32G}}"
pool_slice nightly "${STABILEO_SHARED_CPUS:-}" "${STABILEO_NIGHTLY_CPU_WEIGHT:-20}" "${STABILEO_NIGHTLY_MEMORY_HIGH:-20G}" "${STABILEO_NIGHTLY_MEMORY_MAX:-24G}"
pool_slice timing "$TIMING_CPUS" 100 "${STABILEO_TIMING_MEMORY_HIGH:-14G}" "${STABILEO_TIMING_MEMORY_MAX:-16G}"
[ "$reload" = 0 ] || run systemctl daemon-reload

for N in "$@"; do
  U=sgha$N; D=/home/$U/actions-runner-$N
  log "stabileo runner $N ($U)"
  id "$U" >/dev/null 2>&1 || run useradd -m -U -s /bin/bash "$U"
  if id "$U" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    [ "$(stat -c %a "/home/$U")" = 750 ] || run chmod 750 "/home/$U"
    for g in sudo wheel admin adm lxd docker; do
      if id -nG "$U" | tr ' ' '\n' | grep -qx "$g"; then run gpasswd -d "$U" "$g"; fi
    done
  fi
  [ "$DRY_RUN" = 1 ] || su -s /bin/sh "$U" -c "$PREFLIGHT" || die "runner $N: preflight failed (above); not registering"
  # rustup before config.sh, so ~/.cargo/bin lands in the runner's recorded .path. The jobs pin
  # their own toolchain (rust-toolchain.toml); this is only rustup itself.
  [ -x "/home/$U/.cargo/bin/rustup" ] \
    || run sudo -iu "$U" sh -c 'curl --proto =https --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh -s -- -y --profile minimal --default-toolchain none'
  if ! [ -f "$D/.runner" ]; then
    if [ "$DRY_RUN" = 1 ]; then
      printf '  would register %s (token from stdin)\n' "$(hostname -s)-$U"
    else
      [ -n "$TOKEN" ] || read -r TOKEN || true
      [ -n "$TOKEN" ] || die "runner $N is not registered and no token was given on stdin"
      sudo -iu "$U" bash -c "mkdir -p '$D' && cd '$D' && tar xzf '$TB'"
      printf '%s\n' "$TOKEN" | sudo -u "$U" -H bash -lc \
        'cd "$1" && read -r T && ./config.sh --url "$2" --token "$T" --name "$4-sgha$3" --labels "$5" --unattended --replace' \
        _ "$D" "$REPO_URL" "$N" "$(hostname -s)" "$(labels_of "$N")" | grep -vi token || true
    fi
  fi
  [ -d "$D" ] || continue
  grep -q '^ACTIONS_RUNNER_HOOK_JOB_STARTED=' "$D/.env" 2>/dev/null \
    || run sh -c "echo 'ACTIONS_RUNNER_HOOK_JOB_STARTED=$HOOK' >> '$D/.env'"
  # Build output outside the checkout, so `actions/checkout`'s clean does not throw it away and
  # each job starts warm.
  grep -q '^CARGO_TARGET_DIR=' "$D/.env" 2>/dev/null \
    || run sh -c "echo 'CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/home/$U/cargo-target' >> '$D/.env'"
  # sccache's server listens on one TCP port per host; a runner that reaches another user's
  # server fails every build with "Permission denied (os error 13)".
  grep -q "^SCCACHE_SERVER_PORT=$((4300 + N))\$" "$D/.env" 2>/dev/null \
    || run sh -c "sed -i '/^SCCACHE_SERVER_PORT=/d' '$D/.env' && echo 'SCCACHE_SERVER_PORT=$((4300 + N))' >> '$D/.env'"
  grep -q '^SCCACHE_DIR=' "$D/.env" 2>/dev/null \
    || run sh -c "echo 'SCCACHE_DIR=/home/$U/.cache/sccache' >> '$D/.env'"
  [ -f "$D/.service" ] || run sh -c "cd '$D' && ./svc.sh install '$U'"
  [ -f "$D/.service" ] || continue
  SVC=$(cat "$D/.service")
  POOL=$(pool_of "$N")
  PIN=
  if [ "$POOL" = timing ]; then v=STABILEO_TIMING_CPUS_$N; PIN=${!v}; fi
  if write_file "/etc/systemd/system/$SVC.d/isolation.conf" 644 root:root <<X
[Service]
Slice=stabileo-runners-$POOL.slice
${PIN:+AllowedCPUs=$PIN
}PrivateTmp=true
NoNewPrivileges=true
X
  then
    run systemctl daemon-reload
    # A restart waits for every runner on the host to go idle (guard_runners); a new runner needs none.
    if systemctl is-active -q "$SVC"; then run systemctl restart "$SVC"; fi
  fi
  systemctl is-enabled -q "$SVC" || run systemctl enable "$SVC"
  systemctl is-active -q "$SVC" || run systemctl start "$SVC"
  WATCHDOG_LINES+="$N $(max_minutes_of "$N")"$'\n'
done

[ -d /etc/stabileo-runner ] || run install -d -m 755 -o root -g root /etc/stabileo-runner
printf '%s' "${WATCHDOG_LINES:-}" | write_file "$WATCHDOG_CONF" 644 root:root || true
write_file "$LIBDIR/watchdog.sh" 755 root:root <"$SERVERS_DIR/stabileo-runner-watchdog.sh" || true
reload=0
write_file /etc/systemd/system/stabileo-runner-watchdog.service 644 root:root <<X && reload=1
[Unit]
Description=Restart a hung Stabileo runner

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=$LIBDIR/watchdog.sh
X
write_file /etc/systemd/system/stabileo-runner-watchdog.timer 644 root:root <<'X' && reload=1
[Unit]
Description=Check Stabileo's runners for hung jobs every 5 minutes

[Timer]
OnBootSec=10min
OnUnitActiveSec=5min

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
X
[ "$reload" = 0 ] || run systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl is-enabled -q stabileo-runner-watchdog.timer || run systemctl enable stabileo-runner-watchdog.timer
systemctl is-active -q stabileo-runner-watchdog.timer || run systemctl start stabileo-runner-watchdog.timer
log "stabileo runners ok"
servers/runners-stabileo.sh
servers/elan-home.sh
servers/ai-clis-home.sh
servers/lib.sh
servers/ssh-tailscale-only.sh
servers/nix-gc.sh
servers/services/engines.sh
servers/backup.sh
servers/services/gestion.md
servers/services/lean-cache/refresh.sh
servers/services/lean-cache/measure.sh
servers/services/leanprof-bench.sh
servers/services/leanprof-profile.sh
servers/services/gestion.sh
servers/services/gestion/gestion-sembrar-datos
servers/services/gestion/gestion-eval
servers/services/gestion/gestion-salud
servers/services/gestion/gestion-navegador-puente
servers/services/gestion/gestion-desplegador-aviso
servers/services/gestion/gestion-deploy
servers/services/gestion/gestion-restauracion
servers/services/gestion/gestion-reproduccion
servers/services/gestion/gestion-desplegador
servers/services/perf.sh
servers/services/fuzz-farm.sh
servers/services/lean-cache.sh
servers/services/nix-cache.sh
servers/interactive-first.sh
servers/agent-home.sh
servers/tailscale.sh
servers/stabileo-runner-watchdog.sh
servers/runner-gestion.sh
servers/users.sh
servers/INVENTORY.md
servers/disk-cleanup.sh
servers/dev-home.sh
servers/tailscale-acl.hujson
servers/fuzz-merge-findings.py
servers/runners.sh
servers/apply.sh
servers/disk-health.sh
servers/README.md
servers/memory-guard.sh
servers/prune-clones.sh
servers/base.sh
servers/base-arch.sh
servers/hosts/fede-256gb.env
servers/hosts/concrete-ci-2.env
servers/hosts/concrete-ci-3.env
servers/hosts/stabileo-ci-1.env
servers/monitoring/install.sh
servers/monitoring/concrete-monitor.service
servers/monitoring/README.md
servers/monitoring/concrete-monitor.timer
servers/monitoring/ntfy-send
servers/monitoring/concrete-monitor-failed.service
servers/monitoring/concrete-monitor
servers/keys/laptop.pub
servers/keys/agent_ci_gates.pub
servers/keys/storagebox.known_hosts
servers/keys/fede_admin.pub
servers/keys/desktop.pub
servers/keys/concrete_ci.pub
servers/monitoring/hosts/fede-256gb.conf
servers/monitoring/hosts/concrete-ci-3.conf
servers/monitoring/hosts/concrete-ci-2.conf
servers/monitoring/hosts/stabileo-ci-1.conf

exec
/bin/bash -lc "sed -n '1,115p' servers/README.md; cat servers/apply.sh; sed -n '1,95p' servers/lib.sh; rg -n 'hostname|labels|config.sh' servers/runner-gestion.sh servers/INVENTORY.md servers/base.sh servers/base-arch.sh; bash -n servers/runners.sh; bash --noprofile --norc -lc 'printf \"zero=%s dir=%s url=%s n=%s host=%s pool=%s labels=%s\\n\" \""'$0" "$1" "$2" "$3" "$4" "$5" "$5,$4"'"' _ /home/gha1/actions-runner-1 https://github.com/example/repo 1 concrete-ci-2 concrete" in /tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-dotlabel/src
 succeeded in 0ms:
# servers/

Provisioning for the servers (Concrete's and Stabileo's). Everything machine-level lives here:
users, firewall, sshd, apport, Nix, runners and host roles. The concrete repo
holds only portable engines and tooling (gates, fuzz-farm engine, perf suite,
landing bot, work-queue logic), so host details stay private.

| Host | IP | Role (`hosts/<host>.env`) |
|---|---|---|
| `fede-256gb` (OVH) | 148.113.198.57 | Dev and agent host: tmux + Claude/Codex sessions (`agent`), default `concrete-remote` gate host (`dev`, `CONCRETE_REMOTE=ovh`). No runners. Ubuntu 24.04. |
| `stabileo-ci-1` (Hetzner AX102) | 135.181.130.46 | lambdaclass/stabileo's CI: 14 runners (`stabileo-ci-1-sgha1..14`: 1-8 `stabileo`, 9-10 `stabileo-timing`, 11-14 `stabileo-nightly`), trusted events only. Arch Linux (a NixOS config waits, see "Installing stabileo-ci-1 with NixOS"). |
| `concrete-ci-2` (Hetzner AX102) | 65.109.50.173 | CI + caches: 6 GitHub runners (`gha1..6`) + 2 light (`gha7..8`), Lean seed cache (`lakecache`), Nix binary cache, gate runs (`dev`, `CONCRETE_REMOTE=hetzner`). Arch Linux. |
| `concrete-ci-3` (Hetzner AX102) | 65.108.135.218 | Background work, no runners: fuzz farm (`fuzz`), perf tracking and leanprof profiles (`dev`). Arch Linux. Since 2026-10-26 (see "Background work on concrete-ci-3"). |

SSH and mosh to all four servers go over Tailscale only (MagicDNS names: `fede-256gb`, `stabileo-ci-1`,
`concrete-ci-2`, `concrete-ci-3`); their public IPs answer nothing (`SSH_TAILSCALE_ONLY=1`,
`servers/ssh-tailscale-only.sh`). Emergency access without the tailnet: the Hetzner or OVH web console.

`concrete-ci-1` (Scaleway, 62.210.216.169): deleted 2026-10-23 (see "Moved off Scaleway").

Supported systems: Arch, Debian-family (the apt path; fede-256gb is Ubuntu 24.04) and NixOS
(`nixosConfigurations.stabileo-ci-1` in the flake, not installed yet). **Arch Linux is the default
OS for new servers** (decided 2026-10-22). `base.sh` is the apt path and dispatches to
`base-arch.sh` on Arch.

All run multi-user Nix. The admin is `ubuntu` on fede-256gb (Ubuntu) and `admin`
on Arch (wheel, passwordless sudo, made by `base-arch.sh`), reached with
`ssh -i ~/.ssh/concrete_ci <admin>@<ip>`; root takes keys too on Arch. Interactive work goes through
`ssh concrete-dev` / `ssh concrete-ci2` (aliases in `modules/ssh.nix`, user
`agent`).


Which machine belongs to which project, with IPs and hardware: [INVENTORY.md](INVENTORY.md).

## Layers

1. **Machine** (root): `apply.sh <host>` runs these in order:
   - `base.sh`: apt packages, unattended-upgrades, key-only sshd, ufw (OpenSSH
     plus mosh UDP 60000:60020), no fail2ban (SSH is Tailscale-only), apport off with
     `kernel.core_pattern=core`, gh, and multi-user Nix with flakes.
     On Arch, `base-arch.sh` does the same with pacman (`pacman -Syu` on each
     apply; no unattended upgrades, the monitor alerts when the last upgrade is
     over 14 days old), plus the `admin` user, timesyncd and UTC,
     systemd-coredump off (`kernel.core_pattern=core`, core limit 0 for
     services, user managers and PAM), `/tmp` on disk (`tmp.mount` masked, as
     on Ubuntu), and nix on PATH via `/etc/environment` (Arch's bash skips
     `bash.bashrc` for `ssh host cmd`, which concrete-remote relies on).
   - `users.sh`: `dev`, `agent`, `fuzz` and `lakecache` (each host lists the ones it needs), with the isolation rules
     written at the top of the file.
   - `dev-home.sh`: dev's elan + toolchain, the concrete2 clone with a warm
     `.lake`, devshell gcroots (the `concrete-remote` gate host).
   - `runners.sh`: the CI hosts; runner names are `<hostname>-ghaN`. `RUNNERS` get the label
     `concrete` (CI, the landing tier); `LIGHT_RUNNERS` get `concrete-light` and take only the
     per-push Branch health check, so those ~500 runs a day never queue ahead of a train.
   - `tailscale.sh`: installs Tailscale; it never runs `tailscale up`.
2. **agent's home** (as `agent`): `agent-home.sh` runs home-manager
   `homeConfigurations."agent@<host>"` (`modules/server-home.nix`). That gives
   the Mac's Claude Code settings, commands and agents, its codex config, fish,
   starship, tmux and git, the shared CLI packages, `start-concrete.sh`, and the
   Claude memory sync. Its last step, `elan-home.sh`, installs elan and
   concrete2's lean-toolchain in `~agent/.elan`, so pre-push runs on the host
   include `check_external_checker.sh` instead of skipping it.
3. **Monitoring** (root): `monitoring/` has ntfy health alerts on every host; see
   `monitoring/README.md`.
4. **Services** (root): deployment units for the engines in the concrete repo,
   listed under "Services" below; `apply.sh` runs each `services/<name>.sh` in
   the host's `SERVICES`.

Every script is idempotent, so re-running it changes nothing on a configured
host. `DRY_RUN=1` prints each change instead of making it:

```sh
rsync -a ~/projects/dotfiles/servers/ admin@concrete-ci-2:dotfiles-servers/
ssh admin@concrete-ci-2 'sudo DRY_RUN=1 dotfiles-servers/apply.sh concrete-ci-2'
```

**Never disturb a running CI job.** Package installs and upgrades and
service restarts go through `guard_runners` (`lib.sh`), which waits until no
`Runner.Worker` is running (`RUNNER_WAIT`, default 1 h). Before doing anything
by hand on a runner host, check with
`gh api repos/lambdaclass/concrete/actions/runners -q '.runners[]|"\(.name) \(.busy)"'`
(`CONCRETE_RUNNER_REPO` in the host file; concrete2 until the 2026-11-06 migration).
`base.sh` also sets needrestart to list-only and excludes `actions.runner*`.
On 2026-10-22 an apt install let needrestart restart gha3 mid-job.

No secrets live here. `keys/` holds only public keys. The runner registration
token is passed on stdin (see `runners.sh`). Claude/Codex logins, gh and the
deploy keys are created on the machine and never committed.

## Runners: the toolchain contract

A concrete CI job assumes the host gives it git, a clang that compiles and links C with the
system headers, and a valgrind that starts under `env -i`. The example gates run every binary
under `env -i` (no HOME, no DEBUGINFOD_URLS) so that runs are reproducible. `runners.sh` installs
`/usr/local/lib/concrete-runner/preflight.sh`, which checks exactly that contract. It runs:

- **before a runner registers**: a host that fails it never gets a runner;
- **at the start of every job**, via the job-started hook (`ACTIONS_RUNNER_HOOK_JOB_STARTED` in
  each runner's `.env`), so a broken host fails one job with a one-line cause instead of
  hundreds of gate legs.

Host defects found the hard way, and where each fix lives:

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Trap tests stall at near-zero CPU | apport (Ubuntu) / systemd-coredump (Arch) intercept intentional SIGABRT | `base.sh` / `base-arch.sh`: `kernel.core_pattern=core`, core limit 0 |
| A CI job is killed mid-run | needrestart restarted `actions.runner*` after an apt install | `base.sh`: needrestart list-only; `guard_runners` in `lib.sh` |
| Every native example fails: valgrind "function redirection ... cannot be set up" | Arch strips glibc debug info, and `env -i` hides `DEBUGINFOD_URLS` | `base-arch.sh`: ld.so/libc debug files in `/usr/lib/debug/.build-id`, refreshed by the pacman hook `90-glibc-debuginfo.hook` |
| Every receipt withheld, `Checker: UNIDENTIFIED`; 17 receipt/replay/checker-identity gates fail under concrete-remote (Arch gate host) | Arch keeps `shasum` in `/usr/bin/core_perl`, added only by login shells; concrete-remote's non-login ssh and `nix develop` inherit the pam_env PATH | `base-arch.sh`: perl bin dirs in `/etc/environment` PATH; `shasum` checked by the runner preflight and by `dev-home.sh` in dev's ssh environment |
| `check_mutation_anchors.sh` reports `manifest-rows-match-expected` INERT on the Arch gate host only | non-login ssh on Arch gets no LANG (`/etc/locale.conf` is login-only; sshd accepts no client LANG), so bash `$'\u00b7'` did not expand to UTF-8 | `base-arch.sh`: `LANG=en_US.UTF-8` in `/etc/environment` (what the runners' `.env` has); checked by `dev-home.sh`; concrete spells the anchor as UTF-8 bytes |
| C links fail with `stddef.h` not found (gate host, not runners) | the Lean release's bundled clang came first on the devshell PATH | concrete `flake.nix`: Nix clang before the Lean release |

To debug a runner by hand, run the preflight as its user:
`sudo -u gha3 /usr/local/lib/concrete-runner/preflight.sh`.

#!/bin/bash
# Machine-level setup for one server, in order. Run as root on that host:
#   sudo servers/apply.sh fede-256gb              # apply
#   sudo DRY_RUN=1 servers/apply.sh concrete-ci-2  # show what would change
# Runners need a registration token on stdin (see runners.sh); without one,
# already-registered runners are still checked and fixed up.
# The agent user's home is separate: servers/agent-home.sh, run as agent.
set -euo pipefail
. "$(dirname "$0")/lib.sh"
need_root
[ "$#" -eq 1 ] || die "usage: apply.sh HOST"
# The runner registration token, read ONCE, before any step can consume stdin, and handed to each
# runners.sh call: both pools (RUNNERS, LIGHT_RUNNERS) may need it. Never echoed or written.
RUNNER_TOKEN=""
if [ ! -t 0 ]; then IFS= read -r RUNNER_TOKEN || true; fi
exec </dev/null
load_host "$1"
# base.sh / base-arch.sh run as child processes and read this host setting.
export SSH_TAILSCALE_ONLY="${SSH_TAILSCALE_ONLY:-0}"
[ "$(hostname -s)" = "$1" ] || [ "$DRY_RUN" = 1 ] || die "this is $(hostname -s), not $1"
log "$1: $ROLE"

"$SERVERS_DIR/base.sh"
# shellcheck disable=SC2086
"$SERVERS_DIR/users.sh" $USERS
[[ " $USERS " != *" dev "* ]] || "$SERVERS_DIR/dev-home.sh"
# The runner caps (CONCRETE_RUNNERS_* / CONCRETE_*RUNNER_*) from the host file reach runners.sh.
for v in $(compgen -v | grep -E '^CONCRETE_(LIGHT_)?RUNNERS?_' || true); do export "${v?}"; done
# shellcheck disable=SC2086
[ -z "$RUNNERS" ] || printf '%s\n' "$RUNNER_TOKEN" | "$SERVERS_DIR/runners.sh" $RUNNERS
# shellcheck disable=SC2086
[ -z "${LIGHT_RUNNERS:-}" ] || printf '%s\n' "$RUNNER_TOKEN" | RUNNER_LABEL=concrete-light "$SERVERS_DIR/runners.sh" $LIGHT_RUNNERS
# shellcheck disable=SC2086,SC2046
[ -z "${STABILEO_RUNNERS:-}" ] || printf '%s\n' "$RUNNER_TOKEN" | ( export $(compgen -v STABILEO_)
  "$SERVERS_DIR/runners-stabileo.sh" $STABILEO_RUNNERS ${STABILEO_TIMING_RUNNERS:-} ${STABILEO_NIGHTLY_RUNNERS:-} )
"$SERVERS_DIR/tailscale.sh"
"$SERVERS_DIR/disk-health.sh"
"$SERVERS_DIR/disk-cleanup.sh"
"$SERVERS_DIR/interactive-first.sh"
"$SERVERS_DIR/memory-guard.sh"
"$SERVERS_DIR/backup.sh" "$1"
# Services moved off this host: `services/<name>.sh retire` stops and disables their units and
# keeps their files and state on disk (lib.sh retire_units). Before SERVICES, so a host never
# runs both sides of a move.
for s in ${RETIRED_SERVICES:-}; do
  [ -x "$SERVERS_DIR/services/$s.sh" ] || die "retired service $s: no services/$s.sh"
  "$SERVERS_DIR/services/$s.sh" retire
done
# Deployment units with a script in services/ are applied; the rest are still
# hand-installed on their host (README.md, Services).
for s in $SERVICES; do
  if [ -x "$SERVERS_DIR/services/$s.sh" ]; then "$SERVERS_DIR/services/$s.sh"
  else log "service $s: no services/$s.sh yet (hand-installed)"; fi
done
log "$1 done"
#!/bin/bash
# Shared helpers for the servers/ scripts. Sourced, not run.
#
# Every script here is idempotent: it compares before it changes anything, so a
# re-run on a configured host reports "ok" and changes nothing. DRY_RUN=1 makes
# every mutation print what it would do instead (reads still happen), which is
# how to check a script against a live host without touching it:
#   sudo DRY_RUN=1 servers/apply.sh fede-256gb

DRY_RUN=${DRY_RUN:-0}
SERVERS_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)

log()  { printf '[%s] %s\n' "${0##*/}" "$*"; }
die()  { printf '[%s] ERROR: %s\n' "${0##*/}" "$*" >&2; exit 1; }
need_root() { [ "$(id -u)" -eq 0 ] || [ "$DRY_RUN" = 1 ] || die "run as root"; }

# runners_busy: true while any GitHub Actions runner on this host runs a job.
# A Runner.Worker process exists only for the duration of a job. Same answer
# from anywhere: gh api repos/unbalancedparentheses/concrete2/actions/runners \
#   -q '.runners[]|"\(.name) \(.busy)"'
runners_busy() { pgrep -f '/actions-runner-[0-9]+/bin/Runner\.Worker' >/dev/null 2>&1; }

# guard_runners WHAT: never install/upgrade packages or restart services while
# a runner job is active. On 2026-10-22 an apt install (tailscale.sh) let
# needrestart restart gha3 mid-job and killed a CI run. Waits up to
# RUNNER_WAIT seconds (default 1h) for the runners to go idle, then gives up.
guard_runners() {
  runners_busy || return 0
  if [ "$DRY_RUN" = 1 ]; then printf '  would wait for idle runners before: %s\n' "$1"; return 0; fi
  local waited=0 limit=${RUNNER_WAIT:-3600}
  log "runner jobs active; waiting for idle runners before: $1"
  while runners_busy; do
    [ "$waited" -lt "$limit" ] || die "runners still busy after ${limit}s; not running: $1"
    sleep 30; waited=$((waited + 30))
  done
}

# run CMD...: execute, or print it under DRY_RUN. Package installs/upgrades and
# service restarts go through guard_runners first, so no script here can
# disturb a running CI job.
run() {
  case " $* " in
    *" apt-get install "*|*" apt-get upgrade "*|*" apt-get dist-upgrade "*|*" pacman -S"*|\
    *" systemctl restart "*|*" systemctl reload "*|*" systemctl stop "*|*" --now "*|*"svc.sh stop"*|*"svc.sh start"*|*"svc.sh uninstall"*|*"nix-install.sh"*)
      guard_runners "$*" ;;
  esac
  if [ "$DRY_RUN" = 1 ]; then printf '  would run: %s\n' "$*"; else "$@"; fi
}

# write_file PATH MODE OWNER < content: replace PATH only if the content differs.
# Returns 0 if it changed (or would), 1 if it was already up to date, so
# callers can restart a service only when its config moved.
write_file() {
  local path=$1 mode=$2 owner=$3 tmp
  tmp=$(mktemp)
  cat >"$tmp"
  if [ -f "$path" ] && cmp -s "$tmp" "$path"; then
    rm -f "$tmp"; return 1
  fi
  if [ "$DRY_RUN" = 1 ]; then
    printf '  would write: %s\n' "$path"; rm -f "$tmp"; return 0
  fi
  install -D -m "$mode" -o "${owner%%:*}" -g "${owner##*:}" "$tmp" "$path"
  rm -f "$tmp"
  log "wrote $path"
}

# apt_install PKG...: install only what's missing.
apt_install() {
  local missing=() p
  for p in "$@"; do
    dpkg-query -W -f='${Status}' "$p" 2>/dev/null | grep -q 'install ok installed' || missing+=("$p")
  done
  [ "${#missing[@]}" -eq 0 ] && return 0
  run env DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get install -y "${missing[@]}"
}

# pacman_install PKG...: install only what's missing (Arch).
pacman_install() {
  local missing=() p
  for p in "$@"; do pacman -Qq "$p" >/dev/null 2>&1 || missing+=("$p"); done
  [ "${#missing[@]}" -eq 0 ] && return 0
  run pacman -S --needed --noconfirm "${missing[@]}"
}

# os_id: ID from /etc/os-release: "arch", or "ubuntu"/"debian" for the apt path
# (Debian-family; fede-256gb is Ubuntu). Arch is the default for new servers
# (decided 2026-10-22).
# shellcheck disable=SC1091
os_id() { . /etc/os-release; echo "$ID"; }

# retire_units UNIT...: take a service off this host (apply.sh, RETIRED_SERVICES): disable and stop
# its units. The unit files, the service's user and all its state stay on disk, so the data remains
# for reference and the move can be undone by listing the service in SERVICES again. Stops go
# through run(), so they wait for idle runners like every other restart.
servers/base-arch.sh:41:# Hetzner installimage writes its image name into /etc/hosts; follow hostnamectl.
servers/base-arch.sh:42:if grep -q 'archlinux-latest-64-minimal' /etc/hosts && [ "$(hostname)" != archlinux-latest-64-minimal ]; then
servers/base-arch.sh:43:  run sed -i "s/archlinux-latest-64-minimal/$(hostname)/g" /etc/hosts
servers/runner-gestion.sh:13:# ~ghgestion/actions-runner-gestion, name <hostname>-gestion; instance N>1 is
servers/runner-gestion.sh:14:# ~ghgestion/actions-runner-gestion-N, name <hostname>-gestion-N; each its own systemd unit and
servers/runner-gestion.sh:26:# warns; remove them with `./svc.sh uninstall` + `./config.sh remove --token <removal token>`.
servers/runner-gestion.sh:30:load_host "$(hostname -s)"
servers/runner-gestion.sh:39:HOST=$(hostname -s)
servers/runner-gestion.sh:109:      'cd "$1" && read -r T && ./config.sh --url "$2" --token "$T" --name "$3" --labels gestion --unattended --replace' \
zero=_ dir=/home/gha1/actions-runner-1 url=https://github.com/example/repo n=1 host=concrete-ci-2 pool=concrete labels=concrete,concrete-ci-2

codex
Files were readable. No blocking findings; this is a durable registration change, given the owner-approved backfill of all eight existing runners.

- **Arguments are correct.** `_` becomes `$0`; `$4` is `HOST`, and `$5` is `RUNNER_LABEL`. A harmless Bash probe confirmed `--labels "$5,$4"` produces `concrete,concrete-ci-2`. Default runner labels remain enabled.
- **Hostname is valid and stable for this deployment.** `hosts/concrete-ci-2.env` explicitly requires setting the static hostname, and `apply.sh` checks it against the selected host. `hostname -s` is not universally an immutable identity: renaming a host does not update existing registrations. Here, that same hostname already defines runner names and service identities, so using it as the host label is consistent.
- **Other paths need no matching code change.** Both pools and fresh installs/reinstalls reach the changed registration command. Existing runners skip registration; the stated API backfill covers them. Stabileo and gestión have separate scheduling contracts and need no host label for this Concrete requirement. Toolchain preflight needs no change.
- **README:** mentioning the additional short-hostname label would improve discoverability, but its existing pool-label description remains correct.
- **Comment:** the label description and additive API command are accurate. The workflow/inventory claims cannot be independently verified from this server-only copy. “Runners registered before that date” would be more precise as “the eight existing concrete-ci-2 runners,” matching the supplied migration evidence.

`bash -n servers/runners.sh` passed. No files modified, git commands run, or network used.

